## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Summary: 10 tests, 8 Critical findings, 1 Medium.** This suite is the textbook "coverage-touching" pattern — every production method is called, but almost nothing is verified. That explains the 95% coverage with production bugs.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Tests giving false confidence

#### 1. Systematic Coverage-Touching (suite-wide)

All 10 tests methodically walk the `ProductCatalog` public API in declaration order. Only 3 have any assertion at all, and those are trivial `IsNotNull` checks. This inflates coverage to ~95% while verifying almost zero behavior.

#### 2. No Assertions (5 tests)

These tests execute code and return green — even if the code is completely broken:

| Test | Line | What's unverified |
|------|------|-------------------|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17 | Never checks the product was actually stored |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 31 | Never checks the price actually changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39 | Never checks the product is gone |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 63 | Never checks the count value |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 68 | Never checks prices were reduced |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85 | Never checks products were imported |

**Fix example** — `AddProduct_Works`:
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 17-21)
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// AFTER
var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
```

**Fix example** — `UpdatePrice_Works`:
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 31-36)
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

// AFTER
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
```

**Fix example** — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works`:
```csharp
// BEFORE (line 68-74)
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);

// AFTER
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
